    #       P2 a <pageSetup/> and then a <pageMargins/>, the pageMargins out of
    #          schema order: the same message;
    #       P2C the <pageMargins/> before the <pageSetup/>, the control for P2;
    #       P3 two <headerFooter/>: the same message;
    #       P3C one <headerFooter/>, the control for P3.
    # Each refusal: exit 2, the error line exactly the message the committed
    # source holds, no stdout, no output file. Then the part's messages, read from
    # the source by constant name, compared as SETS with those reached here and
    # those the log states unreachable, each unreachable one with its reason and
    # the tests that cover it; and usage shapes.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 3 P2 from M3 part 3 P1's negative script (printed in
    # records/logs/m3p3-p1/negative.log, byte-identical to its copy kept on the
    # disk as <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p3-p2/gen/negative-template-m3p3-p1.sh;
    # its change lists, P1's HA to HD and the earlier ones, follow below). Every
    # check, control and helper of the frame is that text's. What differs, and
    # why:
    #  IA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects and the build directories
    #      are M3 part 3 P2's. The base is M3 part 3 P1's record commit ("M3 part
    #      3 P1 record:"); the doc commit and the three code commits (the carry,
    #      the crate, the tool) by their full P2 subjects. The spec pin is
    #      specs/0025's blob at P2's doc commit, 6c6e87e3. The working file is
    #      printed, and the status pattern allows it modified: planning holds
    #      "Planning rulings during P2" uncommitted. The pattern allows this
    #      phase's logs and its records/m3p3-p2- and records/m3p3-open- stems.
    #  IB. One family, P0 to P3C, the generator gen-p2.py written for this phase:
    #      the template's sheetData given a tail of root children after it. The
    #      part's write message reached three ways (two pageSetup, one out of
    #      order, two headerFooter), each with its control. P1's apart record of
    #      part 3's two-elements message is dropped: no case here reaches it.
    #  IC. The part's messages are the constants package.rs defines under the
    #      Cargo feature sheetprops, compared as a SET with the constants the six
    #      bodies return: Parts::set_tab_color, set_sheet_view,
    #      set_page_margins, set_page_setup and set_header_footer (the private
    #      fns) and SettingsPass::observe; set_print_options records with no
    #      check and has no private body. "a sheet setting is out of range" and
    #      "a header or footer text is not valid" are stated unreachable through
    #      the tool (the sample's settings and texts are its constants), each
    #      with the crate tests that cover it and each test's body asserted to
    #      hold the message.
    #  ID. Nothing of P1's carried rules is dropped. This script removes no
    #      directory: the worktree goes by git worktree remove, the scratch
    #      directory is kept on the disk under <build>, and no rm of any form is
    #      run (specs/0024 P2 ruling 1 needs none here).
    #
    # P1's text:
    # Milestone 3 part 3 P1 negative.log (specs/0025-sheet-and-print-settings.md,
    # "P1": "The negative log through the binary: the sample on a fixture with two
    # <sheetPr> (refused, with a control)"). One family, --sheetview-sample, the
    # gate's host debug binary copied into a detached worktree of the phase commit
    # and checked against gate.log's hash, on fictional packages this log builds
    # from the phase commit's template files. The template's worksheet holds an
    # empty sheetData alone (no sheetPr, no dimension, no sheetViews), its root
    # binds no relationships prefix:
    #
    # (S) --sheetview-sample:
    #       S0 the bare template: <sheetPr> and <sheetViews> both created, exit 0,
    #          its line;
    #       S1 two <sheetPr/> before the sheetData: the part's new message, "a
    #          worksheet has two sheetPr, ...", from the settings pass;
    #       S1C one <sheetPr/>, the control for S1;
    #       S2 a <dimension> and then a <sheetPr/>, the sheetPr out of schema
    #          order: the same message;
    #       S2C the <sheetPr/> before the <dimension>, the control for S2;
    #       S3 two <sheetViews>, each holding one <sheetView>: part 3's message
    #          for two cols, sheetViews or mergeCells elements;
    #       S3C one <sheetViews>, the control for S3.
    # Each refusal: exit 2, the error line exactly the message the committed
    # source holds, no stdout, no output file. Then the part's messages, read from
    # the source by constant name, compared as SETS with those reached here and
    # those the log states unreachable, the unreachable one with its reason and
    # the test that covers it; and usage shapes.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M3 part 3 P1 from M3 part 2 P3's negative script (printed in
    # records/logs/m3p2-p3/negative.log, byte-identical to its copy kept on the
    # disk under <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p2-p3/scripts, which this phase keeps
    # as <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p3-p1/gen/negative-template-m3p2-p3.sh; its
    # change lists GA to GD stand in that log). Every check, control and helper
    # of the frame is that text's (the entry and exit checks, the shape greps,
    # the role checks, the roots, the gate binary's copy and hash, the message
    # reader messages.py and the body reader returns.py with their controls, the
    # spec lookup, run_bin and its predicates, the set comparison, the usage
    # shapes, the byte count, the status and stderr checks). What differs, and
    # why:
    #  HA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects and the build directories
    #      are M3 part 3 P1's. The base is M3 part 2's close-out record commit
    #      ("M3 part 2 close-out record:"); the doc commit and the three code
    #      commits (the carry, the crate, the tool) by their full P1 subjects.
    #      The spec pin is specs/0025's blob at P1's doc commit, c15d68d2. The
    #      working file is printed, and the status pattern allows it modified:
    #      planning holds "Planning rulings during P1" uncommitted. The pattern
    #      allows this phase's logs and its records/m3p3-p1- and records/m3p3-open-
    #      stems.
    #  HB. One family, S0 to S3C, the generator gen-p1.py written for this phase:
    #      the template's sheetData given a head of root children before it. The
    #      new write message reached two ways (two sheetPr, one out of order),
    #      part 3's message once (two sheetViews), each with its control.
    #  HC. The part's messages are the constants package.rs defines under the
    #      Cargo feature sheetprops (a reader printed below takes each const
    #      whose line follows #[cfg(feature = "sheetprops")]), compared as a SET
    #      with the constants the three bodies return: Parts::set_tab_color,
    #      Parts::set_sheet_view (the private fns) and SettingsPass::observe.
    #      Part 3's two-elements message is recorded apart (as P3 recorded the
    #      index message), since it is not the part's. "a sheet setting is out of
    #      range" is stated unreachable through the tool (the sample's colour and
    #      zoom are its constants), with the crate test that covers it and the
    #      test's body asserted to hold the message. "Errors"' other shared
    #      messages are every edit's, not the sample's constants, and earlier
    #      parts' negative logs reach them; they are printed, not accounted.
    #  HD. Nothing of P3's carried rules is dropped. This script removes no
    #      directory: the worktree goes by git worktree remove, the scratch
    #      directory is kept on the disk under <build>, and no rm of any form is
    #      run (specs/0024 P2 ruling 1 needs none here).
    #
    # Usage: m5p5-p2-negative.sh <phase commit> [<gate log>] > <file outside the
    # tree>; the caller moves the output to records/logs/m5p5-p2/negative.log.
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    SELF=$SELF_DIR/$(basename "$0")
    # specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7: this script's own standard error, kept and counted at the end.
    mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out" || exit 2
    ERR=$SELF_DIR/out/negative.stderr
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    unset EMEND_CORPUS_DIR EMEND_KEEP_DIR RUSTDOCFLAGS RUSTFLAGS CARGO_TARGET_DIR
    # Change MJ: P2 verification ruling 6, and every script's offline cargo
    # setting (this log runs no cargo), each printed as an input line.
    export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
    export CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true
    PHASE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m5p5-p2
    # Change MB: the gate's log and build directory, whose host debug
    # emend-copy copy this log runs.
    GATE_LOG=${2:-$PHASE_DIR/logs/gate.log}
    GATE_BUILD=${GATE_BUILD_ROOT:-$PHASE_DIR/gate}
    GATE_BIN=$GATE_BUILD/bin/host/emend-copy
    BUILD_ROOT=${NEGATIVE_BUILD:-$PHASE_DIR/negative}
    SUPERSEDED_DIR=$PHASE_DIR/superseded
    TARGET_DIR=$PHASE_DIR/target
    SPEC=specs/0036-charts-write-second-set.md
    SPEC_WANT=c98cf950cd4eac30e1d6b37df9380de256910956cd5ac9b160048cce017a9944
    mkdir -p "$BUILD_ROOT" || exit 2
    # Change MP (close-out ruling 1): TMPDIR is <build>/tmp, written
    # <scratch>/tmp, made before any mktemp; every mktemp below takes it.
    TMPDIR=$BUILD_ROOT/tmp
    export TMPDIR
    mkdir -p "$TMPDIR" || exit 2
    # Change HC: this run's own directory, removed at the end (in TMPDIR,
    # change MP).
    B=$(mktemp -d) || exit 2
    git show "$C:scripts/counting.sh" >"$B/counting.sh" || exit 2
    . "$B/counting.sh"
    fail=0
    check() { echo "  $1: $2"; [ "$2" = yes ] || fail=1; }
    yn() { if "$@"; then echo yes; else echo no; fi; }
    # For a condition that must NOT hold: a leading bang inside yn runs a
    # command named by the bang (specs/0001), so a negation has its own helper.
    ynnot() { if "$@"; then echo no; else echo yes; fi; }
    
    head_is() { [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$1" ]; }
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    # The given commit is the phase commit when it is a full sha and HEAD.
    given_ok() { full_sha "$1" && head_is "$1"; }
    if given_ok "$C"; then :; else echo "the phase commit must be a full 40-hex sha that is HEAD, not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    case "${C: -1}" in 0) LAST=1 ;; *) LAST=0 ;; esac
    FAKE_SHA=${C:0:39}$LAST
    SHORT_SHA=${C:0:7}
    # What the status pattern admits (M4 part 2 P1 verification ruling 3; changes
    # NA31 to NA38): this phase's logs, this phase's records (the 3D sample's
    # pair and the open pair, named by the phase commit's short sha, untracked)
    # and planning's modified specs/0036; nothing else.
    OURS="^((\\?\\?| ?[MARCD]) records/logs/m5p5-p2/|\\?\\? records/(m5p5-p2|m5p5-open)-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-$SHORT_SHA[.](md|txt)\$| M specs/0036-charts-write-second-set[.]md\$)"
    entry_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    entry_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    entry_clean() { [ "$entry_all" != error ] && [ "$entry_ours" != error ] && [ "$entry_all" = "$entry_ours" ]; }
    if entry_clean; then :; else
      echo "the working tree holds changes outside this phase's logs, its record pairs and planning's modified spec" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    
    scrub() {
      sed -e "s#$MAIN#<repo>#g" -e "s#$SELF_DIR#<scripts>#g" -e "s#$B#<scratch>/w#g" -e "s#$TMPDIR#<scratch>/tmp#g" \
        -e "s#$BUILD_ROOT#<build>#g" -e "s#$GATE_BUILD#<gatebuild>#g" -e "s#$SUPERSEDED_DIR#<superseded>#g" \
        -e "s#$TARGET_DIR#<target>#g" -e "s#$PHASE_DIR#<phase>#g" \
        -e "s#$HOME#<home>#g"
    }
    exec 3>&1
    exec > >(scrub >&3)
    SCRUB_PID=$!
    
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    echo "invocation: bash <scripts>/$(basename "$0") $*"
    echo "input: RERUN_NOTE: ${RERUN_NOTE:-unset}"
    echo "input: RERUN_FILES: ${RERUN_FILES:-unset}"
    echo "input: PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE: ${PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE:-unset} (exported 1 by this script; P2 verification ruling 6; change MJ)"
    echo "input: CARGO_NET_OFFLINE: ${CARGO_NET_OFFLINE:-unset} (exported true by this script; this log runs no cargo; change MJ)"
    echo "input: TMPDIR=<scratch>/tmp (exported by this script before any mktemp: <build>/tmp, made if missing; close-out ruling 1; change MP)"
    echo "input: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo set || echo unset) (its value never printed)"
    echo "input: HOME: set, read for the paths under it, printed as <home>"
    echo "input: NEGATIVE_BUILD: ${NEGATIVE_BUILD:-unset} (the build root, <build>)"
    echo "input: the gate log: $GATE_LOG (the second argument, or <phase>/logs/gate.log; change MB)"
    echo "input (environment) GATE_BUILD_ROOT: ${GATE_BUILD_ROOT:+set; <gatebuild> below is it, a dry run}${GATE_BUILD_ROOT:-unset, so <gatebuild> is <phase>/gate} (change MB)"
    echo "about: M5 part 5 P2 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    echo
    echo "## the three shape greps, over this script, before its log (specs/0001)"
    D='$'
    SHAPE_CHAIN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) .*(&&|\\|\\|)"
    SHAPE_BANG="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) !"
    SHAPE_ASSIGN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
    P3=python3
    # Change MQ: a Python call is a line that is not a comment where python3
    # is followed by whitespace and an option, `-` or a path ending .py; PYB
    # counts those without `-I -B` after python3.
    PY_CALL="^[[:space:]]*([^#[:space:]].*[^-[:alnum:]_/.])?${P3}[[:space:]]+(-|[^[:space:]]+[.]py)"
    PY_IB="${P3}[[:space:]]+-I[[:space:]]+-B([[:space:]]|\$)"
    # pyb_count <file>: the calls in <file> without -I -B.
    pyb_count() { LC_ALL=C "$G" -E "$PY_CALL" "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -cvE "$PY_IB"; }
    printf '%s\n' "x=${D}(is [ 1 ] && true)" "y=${D}(isnot ! true)" "z=${D}(yn N=1 true)" "  ${P3} -c 'x'" "  ${P3} -I -B -c 'x'" "# ${P3} -c 'x'" "command -v ${P3}" >"$B/shape-fixture"
    echo "command: count_matches -E <shape> <this script>, and the same over a fixture holding one line of each shape; for PYB, the call form then the lines without -I -B"
    for shape in CHAIN BANG ASSIGN PYB; do
      if [ "$shape" = PYB ]; then
        n_self=$(pyb_count "$SELF")
        n_fix=$(pyb_count "$B/shape-fixture")
      else
        var=SHAPE_$shape
        n_self=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$SELF")
        n_fix=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$B/shape-fixture")
      fi
      echo "  shape $shape: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
      check "$shape: this script holds none" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
      check "control: $shape: the same form finds the fixture's one line" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 1 ])"
    done
    n_calls_fix=$(count_matches -E "$PY_CALL" "$B/shape-fixture")
    echo "  Python calls in the fixture by the call form: $n_calls_fix (the one without -I -B and the one with; the comment and command -v are not calls)"
    check "control: the call form counts the fixture's two calls and neither the comment nor command -v" "$(yn [ "$n_calls_fix" = 2 ])"
    check "control: ynnot reports no on a passing command" "$(yn [ "$(ynnot true)" = no ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits by role, read from git"
    by_subject() { git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="$1"; }
    REC=$(by_subject 'M5 part 5 P1 record: logs, the more sample and open records, the check')
    DOC1=$(by_subject 'M5 part 5 P2: commit planning docs (the P1 verification and rulings)')
    CODE1=$(by_subject 'M5 part 5 P2: charts write, the 3D kinds and combined charts')
    CODE2=$(by_subject 'M5 part 5 P2: emend-copy --chart-3d-sample')
    echo "command: git log --format=%H -n 1 -F --grep=<the role's full subject>, for each role"
    echo "  M5 part 5 P1's record commit (the base): ${REC:-none}"
    echo "  the doc commit: ${DOC1:-none}"
    echo "  the crate's code commit: ${CODE1:-none}"
    echo "  the tool's code commit, the phase commit: ${CODE2:-none}"
    echo "command: git rev-parse <phase commit>~0 to <phase commit>~3"
    for k in 0 1 2 3; do git rev-parse "$C~$k"; done | sed 's/^/    /'
    roles_in_order() {
      local r k=0
      for r in "$CODE2" "$CODE1" "$DOC1" "$REC"; do
        [ -n "$r" ] || return 1
        [ "$(git rev-parse "$C~$k")" = "$r" ] || return 1
        k=$((k + 1))
      done
    }
    check "the tool's commit, the crate's, the doc commit and the base, each the next one's parent, the tool's commit the phase commit (changes NA31 to NA38)" "$(yn roles_in_order)"
    roles_ctl() { local CODE2=$CODE1; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the crate's commit named as the phase commit (changes NA31 to NA38)" "$(ynnot roles_ctl)"
    roles_ctl2() { local REC=$DOC1; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit named as the base" "$(ynnot roles_ctl2)"
    echo
    echo "phase: Milestone 5 part 5 P2 ($SPEC) negative.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "rerun: the superseded files are kept in <superseded>"
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")"
        else
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time\n' "$(basename "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"; fi
    fi
    n_cargo=$(pgrep -x cargo | wc -l)
    n_rustc=$(pgrep -x rustc | wc -l)
    echo "SERIALIZED: no other log run was in flight; cargo processes at entry: $n_cargo; rustc processes at entry: $n_rustc; this log builds nothing and runs no cargo: it runs the gate's copied debug emend-copy on fictional fixtures in <scratch>/w (change MB)"
    no_build_running() { [ "$((n_cargo + n_rustc))" = 0 ]; }
    check "no cargo or rustc process was running at entry" "$(yn no_build_running)"
    echo "root: <repo> stands for the repository's top level (inside <home>, so scrubbed first); scripts/counting.sh, the spec, the ten modules crates/emend/src/package.rs, package/sheet_read.rs, package/survey.rs, package/pivot.rs, package/extlink.rs, package/chart.rs, package/chart_write.rs, cells.rs, styles/read.rs and archive.rs (at the phase commit and at the base; package.rs's catalogue read from both; the phase changes chart_write.rs and package.rs but no constant of them), specs/0035-charts-write-first-set.md (at the phase commit, for the messages it quotes), crates/emend/src/package/tests/chart_write.rs (at the phase commit), and tools/emend-copy/tests/null_rewrite.rs (at the phase commit, for the tool tests' fixture and lines) are read from it by git show, and the working spec is hashed and read in it; nothing in it is run, built or written"
    echo "root: <home> stands for the home directory of the account that ran this script"
    echo "root: <phase> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p5-p2, the phase's directory on the disk; <phase>/logs/gate.log is the gate log this log reads for the binary's hash (change MB)"
    echo "root: <scripts> stands for <phase>/scripts, this script's own directory on the disk, which holds the script and, in <scripts>/out, its own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    echo "root: <build> stands for the build root on the disk, <phase>/negative unless NEGATIVE_BUILD names another"
    echo "root: <gatebuild> stands for <phase>/gate (GATE_BUILD_ROOT in a dry run), the gate log's build directory; <gatebuild>/bin/host/emend-copy is the gate's copy of its host debug emend-copy, copied from there and never run in place; read only (change MB)"
    echo "root: <superseded> stands for <phase>/superseded, where a rerun's superseded files are kept; read only"
    echo "root: <scratch>/tmp stands for <build>/tmp, this run's TMPDIR, exported before any mktemp and kept (change MP)"
    echo "root: <scratch>/w stands for this run's mktemp -d working directory, made in <scratch>/tmp, removed by this script at its end (change HC, kept; change MP): <scratch>/w/counting.sh the phase commit's library, sourced; <scratch>/w/bin the copied binary; <scratch>/w/null_rewrite.rs the tool tests' source; <scratch>/w/fx the fictional fixtures (changes NE31 to NE38); <scratch>/w/out the outputs; the message and catalogue readers, the fixture generator and the captured outputs (*.stdout, *.stderr, *.out)"
    echo "root: <target> stands for <phase>/target, the phase's one target root (specs/0001); this log builds nothing and reads and writes nothing under it"
    echo "root: <close> stands for a directory of an earlier phase's log and appears in this log only in the printed script's carried history; this log reads and writes nothing under it (change LD, kept)"
    apart() { case "$1/" in "$2"/*) return 1 ;; esac; case "$2/" in "$1"/*) return 1 ;; esac; return 0; }
    roots_distinct() { apart "$BUILD_ROOT" "$MAIN" && apart "$BUILD_ROOT" "$SELF_DIR" && apart "$MAIN" "$SELF_DIR" && apart "$SUPERSEDED_DIR" "$SELF_DIR" && apart "$SUPERSEDED_DIR" "$BUILD_ROOT" && apart "$SUPERSEDED_DIR" "$MAIN" && apart "$TARGET_DIR" "$BUILD_ROOT" && apart "$TARGET_DIR" "$MAIN" && apart "$TARGET_DIR" "$SELF_DIR" && apart "$GATE_BUILD" "$BUILD_ROOT" && apart "$GATE_BUILD" "$MAIN" && apart "$GATE_BUILD" "$SELF_DIR" && apart "$GATE_BUILD" "$TARGET_DIR"; }
    check "the roots other than <home> and <phase> are distinct, none inside another (<scratch>/w inside <build>)" "$(yn roots_distinct)"
    roots_ctl() { apart "$B" "$BUILD_ROOT"; }
    check "control: apart refuses <scratch>/w against <build>, which holds it" "$(ynnot roots_ctl)"
    # under_tmpdir <dir>: <dir> lies inside TMPDIR (change MP).
    under_tmpdir() { case "$1/" in "$TMPDIR"/?*) return 0 ;; esac; return 1; }
    echo "TMPDIR: <scratch>/tmp; this run's mktemp -d directory: <scratch>/w"
    check "this run's mktemp -d directory lies under TMPDIR (close-out ruling 1)" "$(yn under_tmpdir "$B")"
    check "control: under_tmpdir refuses <build>, which holds TMPDIR" "$(ynnot under_tmpdir "$BUILD_ROOT")"
    check "control: under_tmpdir refuses TMPDIR itself" "$(ynnot under_tmpdir "$TMPDIR")"
    check "control: under_tmpdir refuses a directory outside it, <phase>" "$(ynnot under_tmpdir "$PHASE_DIR")"
    echo "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set in this shell: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    key_unset() { [ -z "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ]; }
    check "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set" "$(yn key_unset)"
    key_set_ctl() { local ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=planted; key_unset; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a shell where the variable is set" "$(ynnot key_set_ctl)"
    echo "at entry: status lines $entry_all; of them admitted by the phase's pattern (this phase's logs, its records, planning's modified specs/0036) $entry_ours; the lines:"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
    echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    echo "  the controls' commits: the null commit $NULL_SHA; the fabricated commit $FAKE_SHA (the given one, its last hex digit changed); the short sha $SHORT_SHA"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is a full sha" "$(yn full_sha "$C")"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(yn head_is "$C")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the null commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$NULL_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a fabricated commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$FAKE_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a short sha of the real commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$SHORT_SHA")"
    short_names_head() { [ "$(git rev-parse "$SHORT_SHA")" = "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" ]; }
    check "control: the short sha is the real commit's, so only its form is refused" "$(yn short_names_head)"
    ours_ctl() { printf ' M scripts/check.sh\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified gate file" "$(ynnot ours_ctl)"
    ours_src_ctl() { printf ' M crates/emend/Cargo.toml\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified manifest" "$(ynnot ours_src_ctl)"
    ours_cl_ctl() { printf ' M CHANGELOG.md\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified CHANGELOG.md" "$(ynnot ours_cl_ctl)"
    ours_roadmap_ctl() { printf ' M ROADMAP.md\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified ROADMAP.md (committed and clean in this phase)" "$(ynnot ours_roadmap_ctl)"
    ours_rec_ctl() { printf '?? records/logs/m5p5-p2/gate.log\n?? records/m5p5-p2-2026-10-14-%s.md\n?? records/m5p5-p2-2026-10-14-%s.txt\n?? records/m5p5-open-2026-10-14-%s.md\n M specs/0036-charts-write-second-set.md\n?? records/logs/m5p5-p1/gate.log\n?? records/logs/m5p5-p2x/gate.log\n?? records/m5p5-p2-2026-10-14-abcdef0.md\n?? records/m5p5-p1-2026-10-14-%s.md\n?? records/m5p5-p2-3d-2026-10-14-%s.md\n M ROADMAP.md\n?? specs/0036-charts-write-second-set.md\n M specs/0035-charts-write-first-set.md\n' "$SHORT_SHA" "$SHORT_SHA" "$SHORT_SHA" "$SHORT_SHA" "$SHORT_SHA" | count_matches -E "$OURS" /dev/stdin; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern admits this phase's log, its untracked 3D-sample and open records and planning's modified specs/0036 alone; it refuses P1's log directory and record stem, a sibling directory, a record of another commit, a sample stem this phase does not write, ROADMAP.md, an untracked spec and a modified specs/0035 (changes NA31 to NA38)" "$(yn [ "$(ours_rec_ctl)" = 5 ])"
    SPEC_HAVE=$(sha256sum <"$SPEC" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    SPEC_BLOB=$(git show "$C:$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$SPEC | sha256sum: $SPEC_BLOB; sha256sum $SPEC (the working file, printed and not asserted: planning holds its rulings during P2 uncommitted; changes NA31 to NA38): $SPEC_HAVE"
    check "the spec's blob at the phase commit is at the hash this log pins" "$(yn [ "$SPEC_BLOB" = "$SPEC_WANT" ])"
    spec_ctl() { [ "$(printf 'x' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" = "$SPEC_WANT" ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the hash of another file" "$(ynnot spec_ctl)"
    echo
    echo "## script that wrote this log"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$SELF"
    echo
    echo "## the shared counting library this log sources"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/counting.sh"
    echo
    echo "## counting controls"
    counting_controls
    if [ "$counting_controls_ok" != yes ]; then fail=1; fi
    echo
    echo "## the gate's debug emend-copy, copied into <scratch>/w/bin and checked against gate.log (change MB)"
    sha_of() { sha256sum <"$1" | cut -d' ' -f1; }
    gate_log_there() { [ -s "$GATE_LOG" ]; }
    check "the gate log is there and not empty" "$(yn gate_log_there)"
    HASH_FORM='^  <build>/bin/host/emend-copy: sha256 [0-9a-f]{64}, bytes [0-9]+$'
    nhash=$(count_matches -E "$HASH_FORM" "$GATE_LOG")
    GATED=$(sed -n -E 's#^  <build>/bin/host/emend-copy: sha256 ([0-9a-f]{64}), bytes [0-9]+$#\1#p' "$GATE_LOG" | head -n 1)
    echo "command: count_matches -E and sed for the hash line of the gate's host emend-copy copy in the gate log (sha256 $(sha_of "$GATE_LOG")): lines $nhash; hash ${GATED:-none}"
    check "gate.log holds exactly one hash line for its copy <build>/bin/host/emend-copy" "$(yn [ "$nhash" = 1 ])"
    printf '  <build>/bin/host/emend-copy: sha256 %s, bytes 1\n  <build>/bin/i686/emend-copy: sha256 %s, bytes 1\n' \
      "$(printf 'a' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$(printf 'b' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" >"$B/c-gate.log"
    check "control: the same form counts one line in a fixture holding a host and an i686 line" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -E "$HASH_FORM" "$B/c-gate.log")" = 1 ])"
    echo "command: mkdir <scratch>/w/bin; cp <gatebuild>/bin/host/emend-copy <scratch>/w/bin/emend-copy"
    mkdir "$B/bin" || exit 2
    cp "$GATE_BIN" "$B/bin/emend-copy"
    BIN=$B/bin/emend-copy
    echo "  <scratch>/w/bin/emend-copy: sha256 $(sha_of "$BIN"), bytes $(wc -c <"$BIN")"
    gated_found() { [ -n "$GATED" ]; }
    check "control: the reader found a hash in gate.log" "$(yn gated_found)"
    bin_is_gated() { gated_found && [ "$(sha_of "$BIN")" = "$GATED" ]; }
    check "the copied binary is the one gate.log hashed, not a rebuild" "$(yn bin_is_gated)"
    bin_ctl() { local GATED; GATED=$(printf 'x' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1); bin_is_gated; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses another hash" "$(ynnot bin_ctl)"
    echo
    echo "## every mktemp call, this script's and the counting library's (ruling 12; change MW, carried as NB3 and NB31 to NB38)"
    MK=mktemp
    # A call is a line that is not a comment holding a command substitution of
    # mktemp; a call in TMPDIR's form takes no argument but -d (no -p, no
    # --tmpdir, no -t and no template), so mktemp puts it in TMPDIR.
    MK_CALL="^[^#]*[$][(]${MK}([[:space:]]|[)])"
    MK_FORM="[$][(]${MK}( -d)?[)]"
    # mk_calls <file>: the calls; mk_bad <file>: the calls not in that form.
    mk_calls() { count_matches -E "$MK_CALL" "$1"; }
    mk_bad() { LC_ALL=C "$G" -E "$MK_CALL" "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -cvE "$MK_FORM"; }
    printf '%s\n' "a=${D}(${MK} -d) || exit 2" "b=${D}(${MK} -p /x)" "# c=${D}(${MK} -p /y)" "d=${D}(${MK})" "echo ${MK} -d" >"$B/c-mktemp"
    for f in "$SELF" "$B/counting.sh"; do
      name=$([ "$f" = "$SELF" ] && echo "this script" || echo "the counting library, <scratch>/w/counting.sh")
      echo "  $name: mktemp calls $(mk_calls "$f"); of them not in TMPDIR's form $(mk_bad "$f")"
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -E "$MK_CALL" "$f" | sed 's/^[[:space:]]*/    /'
    done
    check "this script holds one mktemp call, B's mktemp -d, in TMPDIR's form, and makes no plain file" "$(yn [ "$(mk_calls "$SELF")$(mk_bad "$SELF")" = 10 ])"
    check "the counting library's mktemp calls (one, its controls' directory, removed by it) are each in TMPDIR's form" "$(yn [ "$(mk_bad "$B/counting.sh")" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same count finds the fixture's three calls, not its comment or its echo" "$(yn [ "$(mk_calls "$B/c-mktemp")" = 3 ])"
    check "control: the same form refuses the fixture's one call with -p" "$(yn [ "$(mk_bad "$B/c-mktemp")" = 1 ])"
    echo "  the library's directory is made after TMPDIR is exported (change MP), so it lies under TMPDIR as <scratch>/w does, whose place is checked above"
    
    echo
    echo "## the messages, read from the phase commit's source (changes NC31 to NC38)"
    TAB=$(printf '\t')
    cat >"$B/messages.py" <<'PY'
    """The Error::Package messages of a Rust source file, by constant name, one
    per line as NAME<TAB>message in source order; a constant with or without
    pub(crate). With --name N, only N.
    Usage: messages.py <file.rs> [--name N]."""
    import re
    import sys
    
    text = open(sys.argv[1]).read()
    found = re.findall(r'^(?:pub\(crate\) )?const ([A-Z_0-9]+): Error =\s*Error::Package\(\s*"([^"]*)",?\s*\);',
                       text, re.M)
    args = sys.argv[2:]
    if args[:1] == ["--name"]:
        found = [(n, m) for n, m in found if n == args[1]]
    for n, m in found:
        print("%s\t%s" % (n, m))
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/messages.py"
    MODULES="crates/emend/src/package.rs crates/emend/src/package/sheet_read.rs crates/emend/src/package/survey.rs crates/emend/src/package/pivot.rs crates/emend/src/package/extlink.rs crates/emend/src/package/chart.rs crates/emend/src/package/chart_write.rs crates/emend/src/cells.rs crates/emend/src/styles/read.rs crates/emend/src/archive.rs"
    : >"$B/all-now.tsv"
    : >"$B/all-base.tsv"
    # in_base <path>: the base's tree holds the file (git ls-tree prints its
    # name, and nothing for a file it lacks).
    in_base() { [ "$(git ls-tree --name-only "$REC" -- "$1")" = "$1" ]; }
    # in_phase <path>: the phase commit's tree holds the file.
    in_phase() { [ "$(git ls-tree --name-only "$C" -- "$1")" = "$1" ]; }
    echo "command: for each of the ten modules, git show <commit>:<module> at the phase commit and at the base, and python3 -I -B <scratch>/w/messages.py over each copy"
    for f in $MODULES; do
      stem=$(basename "$f" .rs)
      git show "$C:$f" >"$B/now-$stem.rs"
      if in_base "$f"; then git show "$REC:$f" >"$B/base-$stem.rs"; else : >"$B/base-$stem.rs"; fi
      python3 -I -B "$B/messages.py" "$B/now-$stem.rs" >"$B/now-$stem.tsv"
      python3 -I -B "$B/messages.py" "$B/base-$stem.rs" >"$B/base-$stem.tsv"
      cat "$B/now-$stem.tsv" >>"$B/all-now.tsv"
      cat "$B/base-$stem.tsv" >>"$B/all-base.tsv"
      echo "  $f: in the base's tree $(yn in_base "$f"); constants at the phase commit $(count_lines "$B/now-$stem.tsv"), at the base $(count_lines "$B/base-$stem.tsv")"
    done
    all_in_base() { local f; for f in $MODULES; do in_base "$f" || return 1; done; }
    check "the base holds each of the ten modules (changes NC35 to NC38)" "$(yn all_in_base)"
    check "control: in_base says no for a module path no tree holds" "$(ynnot in_base crates/emend/src/planted.rs)"
    LC_ALL=C sort -u "$B/all-now.tsv" >"$B/all-now.set"
    LC_ALL=C sort -u "$B/all-base.tsv" >"$B/all-base.set"
    echo "  constants with their messages: at the phase commit $(count_lines "$B/all-now.set"); at the base $(count_lines "$B/all-base.set")"
    same_messages() { [ "$(count_lines "$B/all-base.set")" -ge 1 ] && cmp -s "$B/all-now.set" "$B/all-base.set"; }
    check "the phase adds, removes and rewords no Error::Package constant of the ten modules the base holds, the chart writer's among them, though it changes chart_write.rs and package.rs (changes NC35 to NC38)" "$(yn same_messages)"
    printf 'PLANTED\tplanted\n' | LC_ALL=C sort -u - "$B/all-now.tsv" >"$B/c-now-plus.set"
    plant_ctl() { cmp -s "$B/c-now-plus.set" "$B/all-base.set"; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a set with a planted constant" "$(ynnot plant_ctl)"
    # Change NC32, kept by NC34 and NC35: chart.rs is in the base since part 3
    # P1 and among the ten above; its one constant keeps the base's message.
    echo "command: <scratch>/w/now-chart.tsv and <scratch>/w/base-chart.tsv, written by the loop above (crates/emend/src/package/chart.rs at the phase commit and at the base)"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/now-chart.tsv"
    nchart=$(count_lines "$B/now-chart.tsv")
    CHART_TEXT=$(awk -F"$TAB" '$1 == "CHART_UNREADABLE" { print $2 }' "$B/now-chart.tsv")
    CHART_BASE=$(awk -F"$TAB" '$1 == "CHART_UNREADABLE" { print $2 }' "$B/base-chart.tsv")
    chart_one() { [ "$nchart" = 1 ] && [ -n "$CHART_TEXT" ] && [ "$CHART_TEXT" = "$CHART_BASE" ]; }
    check "the chart module holds exactly one Error::Package constant, CHART_UNREADABLE, with the message the base's chart.rs holds (change NC32)" "$(yn chart_one)"
    chart_ctl() { local CHART_BASE=planted; chart_one; }
    check "control: the same test refuses a planted base message" "$(ynnot chart_ctl)"
    printf 'const A: Error = Error::Package("x");\npub(crate) const B: Error =\n    Error::Package("two");\nconst C: Error = Error::Package(\n    "three",\n);\n' >"$B/c-msgs.rs"
    python3 -I -B "$B/messages.py" "$B/c-msgs.rs" --name B >"$B/c-name.tsv"
    python3 -I -B "$B/messages.py" "$B/c-msgs.rs" --name C >>"$B/c-name.tsv"
    check "control: --name takes the one constant named, pub(crate) and wrapped or multi-line" "$(yn [ "$(cut -f2 "$B/c-name.tsv" | tr '\n' ' ')" = "two three " ])"
    # Change NC35: the part's module, chart_write.rs, in the base since P1 and
    # among the ten above, holds the part's four messages and no other
    # constant, as at the base.
    WRITE_RS=crates/emend/src/package/chart_write.rs
    cp "$B/now-chart_write.tsv" "$B/part.tsv"
    echo "command: <scratch>/w/now-chart_write.tsv, written by the loop above ($WRITE_RS at the phase commit; change NC35)"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/part.tsv"
    check "the base's tree and the phase commit's each hold $WRITE_RS (change NC35)" "$(yn [ "$(yn in_base "$WRITE_RS")$(yn in_phase "$WRITE_RS")" = yesyes ])"
    PART_NAMES="CHART_TEXT_INVALID CHART_OPTION_KIND CHART_SIZE_ANCHOR CHART_ANCHOR_OUT_OF_RANGE"
    part_names() { cut -f1 "$B/part.tsv" | LC_ALL=C sort | tr '\n' ' '; }
    PART_WANT=$(printf '%s\n' $PART_NAMES | LC_ALL=C sort | tr '\n' ' ')
    part_four() { [ "$(count_lines "$B/part.tsv")" = 4 ] && [ "$(part_names)" = "$PART_WANT" ] && [ "$(awk -F"$TAB" '$2 == "" { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/part.tsv")" = 0 ]; }
    check "chart_write.rs holds exactly the four constants of the part, CHART_TEXT_INVALID, CHART_OPTION_KIND, CHART_SIZE_ANCHOR and CHART_ANCHOR_OUT_OF_RANGE, none empty (changes NC34 and NC35)" "$(yn part_four)"
    part_ctl() { local PART_WANT="CHART_ANCHOR_OUT_OF_RANGE CHART_OPTION_KIND CHART_SIZE_ANCHOR PLANTED "; part_four; }
    check "control: the same test refuses a planted name in place of one of the four" "$(ynnot part_ctl)"
    # Change NC37 (from NC35 and NC36; P1 verification ruling G): each of the
    # four is a list item of the package header's catalogue at the phase commit
    # and at the base alike: part 4 P2 wrote the catalogue, and this phase adds
    # no message (the catalogue for this part is P3's). Read as the crate's
    # catalogue test reads a list item.
    cat >"$B/catalogue.py" <<'PY'
    """The messages a Rust source file's catalogue lists: each //! line whose
    text, trimmed, starts '- "', its string read to the closing quote, the
    escaped brackets unescaped, one per line, as the crate's catalogue test
    reads them.
    Usage: catalogue.py <file.rs>."""
    import re
    import sys
    
    for line in open(sys.argv[1]):
        m = re.match(r'^\s*//!\s*- "((?:[^"\\]|\\.)*)"', line)
        if m:
            print(m.group(1).replace("\\[", "[").replace("\\]", "]"))
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/catalogue.py"
    python3 -I -B "$B/catalogue.py" "$B/now-package.rs" >"$B/cat-now.txt"
    python3 -I -B "$B/catalogue.py" "$B/base-package.rs" >"$B/cat-base.txt"
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <scratch>/w/catalogue.py over crates/emend/src/package.rs at the phase commit and at the base: list items $(count_lines "$B/cat-now.txt") and $(count_lines "$B/cat-base.txt") (changes NC36 and NC37)"
    # in_catalogue <NAME> <list>: the constant's message is one whole line of
    # the list.
    in_catalogue() { local m; m=$(awk -F"$TAB" -v n="$1" '$1 == n { print $2 }' "$B/part.tsv"); [ -n "$m" ] && [ "$(count_matches -xF "$m" "$2")" = 1 ]; }
    for name in $PART_NAMES; do
      echo "  $name: in the catalogue at the phase commit $(yn in_catalogue "$name" "$B/cat-now.txt"); at the base $(yn in_catalogue "$name" "$B/cat-base.txt")"
      check "$name's message is a list item of the package header's catalogue at the phase commit, once, and at the base, once (changes NC36 and NC37; P1 verification ruling G)" "$(yn [ "$(yn in_catalogue "$name" "$B/cat-now.txt")$(yn in_catalogue "$name" "$B/cat-base.txt")" = yesyes ])"
    done
    check "control: in_catalogue says no for a constant the module does not hold" "$(ynnot in_catalogue PLANTED_NAME "$B/cat-now.txt")"
    awk -v m="$(awk -F"$TAB" '$1 == "CHART_TEXT_INVALID" { print $2 }' "$B/part.tsv")" '$0 != m' "$B/cat-base.txt" >"$B/c-cat-base.txt"
    check "control: in_catalogue says no for CHART_TEXT_INVALID against the base's list with its line removed (change NC36)" "$(ynnot in_catalogue CHART_TEXT_INVALID "$B/c-cat-base.txt")"
    printf '//! - "a planted \\[message\\]" (`some_test`).\n//! "not a list item"\n' >"$B/c-cat.rs"
    cat_ctl() { [ "$(python3 -I -B "$B/catalogue.py" "$B/c-cat.rs")" = "a planted [message]" ]; }
    check "control: catalogue.py reads a list item, its brackets unescaped, and not a plain doc line" "$(yn cat_ctl)"
    : >"$B/known.tsv"
    # Change NC37: N3's message and part 1's three are read beside N1's and N2's.
    KNOWN="DRAWING_UNREADABLE TWO_DRAWINGS NO_SUCH_PART CELL_EDIT_REPLACED REMOVED_PART_EDITED"
    for name in $KNOWN; do
      python3 -I -B "$B/messages.py" "$B/now-package.rs" --name "$name" >>"$B/known.tsv"
    done
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <scratch>/w/messages.py <scratch>/w/now-package.rs --name <NAME>, for each of $KNOWN (at the phase commit; changes NC34 to NC37)"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/known.tsv"
    nknown=$(count_lines "$B/known.tsv")
    nempty=$(awk -F"$TAB" '$2 == "" { n++ } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/known.tsv")
    known_ok() { [ "$nknown" = 5 ] && [ "$nempty" = 0 ] && [ "$(cut -f1 "$B/known.tsv" | tr '\n' ' ')" = "$KNOWN " ]; }
    check "the five messages read apart, N1's and N2's, N3's and part 1's three, are each read once, in order, not empty (change NC37)" "$(yn known_ok)"
    known_ctl() { local KNOWN="DRAWING_UNREADABLE TWO_DRAWINGS NO_SUCH_PART CELL_EDIT_REPLACED PLANTED_NAME"; known_ok; }
    check "control: known_ok refuses a planted name in place of one of the five" "$(ynnot known_ctl)"
    # msg <NAME>: the message the source holds for the constant, as the tool
    # prints it.
    msg() { awk -F"$TAB" -v n="$1" '$1 == n { print "error: " $2 }' "$B/known.tsv"; }
    msg_ctl() { [ -z "$(msg PLANTED_NAME)" ]; }
    check "control: msg gives nothing for a constant the source does not hold" "$(yn msg_ctl)"
    # Change NC37: specs/0036 quotes three of the four call messages and none
    # of the drawing or part 1 messages ("At the write, the drawing's messages
    # as part 4 says"); specs/0035 at the phase commit quotes N1's to N3's and
    # the four. Part 1's three are printed, not asserted.
    PART4_SPEC=specs/0035-charts-write-first-set.md
    git show "$C:$SPEC" >"$B/spec-committed.md"
    git show "$C:$PART4_SPEC" >"$B/spec-part4.md"
    cat "$B/known.tsv" "$B/part.tsv" >"$B/quoted.tsv"
    python3 -I -B - "$B/quoted.tsv" "$B/spec-part4.md" "$B/spec-committed.md" "$SPEC" >"$B/in-spec.tsv" <<'PY'
    import re
    import sys
    part4 = re.sub(r"\s+", " ", open(sys.argv[2]).read())
    committed = re.sub(r"\s+", " ", open(sys.argv[3]).read())
    working = re.sub(r"\s+", " ", open(sys.argv[4]).read())
    for line in open(sys.argv[1]):
        name, message = line.rstrip("\n").split("\t", 1)
        print("%s\tspec0035=%s\tcommitted=%s\tworking=%s" % (name, "yes" if message in part4 else "no",
                                                            "yes" if message in committed else "no",
                                                            "yes" if message in working else "no"))
    PY
    echo "command: each message looked for in $PART4_SPEC (git show <phase commit>), in the committed $SPEC (git show <phase commit>) and in its working file, whitespace folded (change NC37)"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/in-spec.tsv"
    QUOTED4="^(DRAWING_UNREADABLE|TWO_DRAWINGS|CHART_TEXT_INVALID|CHART_OPTION_KIND|CHART_SIZE_ANCHOR|CHART_ANCHOR_OUT_OF_RANGE)${TAB}spec0035=yes${TAB}"
    QUOTED="^(CHART_TEXT_INVALID|CHART_OPTION_KIND|CHART_ANCHOR_OUT_OF_RANGE)${TAB}spec0035=yes${TAB}committed=yes${TAB}working=yes\$"
    quoted4_ok() { [ "$(count_matches -E "$QUOTED4" "$B/in-spec.tsv")" = 6 ]; }
    quoted_ok() { [ "$(count_matches -E "$QUOTED" "$B/in-spec.tsv")" = 3 ]; }
    check "N1's and N2's message, N3's and the part's four are each quoted in $PART4_SPEC at the phase commit (change NC37)" "$(yn quoted4_ok)"
    check "the three call messages specs/0036 quotes (CHART_TEXT_INVALID, CHART_OPTION_KIND and CHART_ANCHOR_OUT_OF_RANGE) are each quoted in its committed and its working file (change NC37)" "$(yn quoted_ok)"
    printf 'CHART_OPTION_KIND\tspec0035=yes\tcommitted=yes\tworking=no\nCHART_TEXT_INVALID\tspec0035=yes\tcommitted=yes\tworking=yes\nTWO_DRAWINGS\tspec0035=no\tcommitted=no\tworking=no\n' >"$B/c-in-spec.tsv"
    check "control: the same count finds one line where one of two says working=no" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -E "$QUOTED" "$B/c-in-spec.tsv")" = 1 ])"
    check "control: the part 4 count finds two lines where a third says spec0035=no" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -E "$QUOTED4" "$B/c-in-spec.tsv")" = 2 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the tests that cover the cases (changes ND31 to ND38)"
    COVER_DRAWING=the_drawing_refusals_are_the_image_writer_s
    COVER_TOOL=the_chart_kinds_sample_refuses_a_drawing_whose_root_is_not_ws_dr_and_leaves_nothing
    COVER_LINE=the_chart_kinds_sample_adds_one_chart_of_each_kind_and_reads_them_back
    COVER_ADD_TOOL=the_add_chart_sample_refuses_a_drawing_relationship_with_no_part_and_leaves_nothing
    COVER_ADD_LINE=the_add_chart_sample_adds_a_column_chart_and_reads_it_back
    COVER_TEXT=the_text_rules_refuse_each_field_and_record_nothing
    COVER_OPTION=a_chart_with_no_series_is_refused
    COVER_OPTION_BAR=each_bar_grouping_writes_overlap_when_stacked
    COVER_OPTION_LINE=a_line_chart_takes_each_grouping_but_clustered
    COVER_OPTION_AREA=an_area_chart_takes_each_grouping_but_clustered
    COVER_OPTION_PIE=a_pie_with_two_series_or_an_axis_title_is_refused
    COVER_SIZE=each_anchor_form_with_its_size
    COVER_ANCHOR=the_size_and_anchor_rules_refuse_and_record_nothing
    # Change ND37: N3's tool test, part 1's messages' crate test, and this
    # phase's tests for the new rules.
    COVER_TWO_TOOL=the_add_chart_sample_refuses_a_worksheet_with_two_drawing_elements_and_leaves_nothing
    COVER_PARTS=a_chart_on_a_removed_replaced_or_added_part_is_refused
    COVER_OPTION_DOUGHNUT=a_doughnut_s_hole_outside_1_to_90_or_an_axis_title_is_refused
    COVER_OPTION_STOCK=a_stock_chart_with_two_or_five_series_is_refused
    COVER_SIZES=sizes_missing_on_a_bubble_series_or_given_on_another_plot_are_refused
    # Change ND38: N4's tool test, B2's line's tool test, and this phase's
    # tests for the new rules.
    COVER_3D_TOOL=the_chart_3d_sample_refuses_a_drawing_whose_root_is_not_ws_dr_and_leaves_nothing
    COVER_3D_LINE=the_chart_3d_sample_adds_the_3d_kinds_and_a_combined_chart_and_reads_them_back
    COVER_OPTION_LINE3D=a_line_3d_chart_takes_each_grouping_but_clustered_with_the_series_axis
    COVER_OPTION_AREA3D=an_area_3d_chart_takes_each_grouping_but_clustered
    COVER_OPTION_PIE3D=a_pie_3d_chart_is_written_and_refused_as_a_pie
    COVER_COMBINED_FIRST=a_scatter_first_plot_a_same_variant_second_or_a_scatter_on_the_primary_axes_is_refused
    COVER_COMBINED_NO_AXES=a_pie_or_another_plot_with_no_axes_and_a_combined_plot_is_refused
    COVER_COMBINED_3D_SECOND=a_combined_3d_second_plot_is_refused
    COVER_COMBINED_3D_FIRST=a_combined_3d_first_plot_is_refused
    COVER_COMBINED_SECONDARY=a_secondary_title_or_format_without_the_secondary_axis_is_refused
    COVER_COMBINED_ORDER=the_combined_rules_and_texts_follow_the_check_order
    P2_OPTION="COVER_OPTION_LINE3D COVER_OPTION_AREA3D COVER_OPTION_PIE3D COVER_COMBINED_FIRST COVER_COMBINED_NO_AXES COVER_COMBINED_3D_SECOND COVER_COMBINED_3D_FIRST COVER_COMBINED_SECONDARY COVER_COMBINED_ORDER"
    git show "$C:crates/emend/src/package/tests/chart_write.rs" >"$B/write-tests.rs"
    git show "$C:tools/emend-copy/tests/null_rewrite.rs" >"$B/null_rewrite.rs"
    echo "command: count_matches -F 'fn <name>()' over crates/emend/src/package/tests/chart_write.rs and tools/emend-copy/tests/null_rewrite.rs at the phase commit"
    for name in COVER_DRAWING COVER_TEXT COVER_OPTION COVER_OPTION_BAR COVER_OPTION_LINE COVER_OPTION_AREA COVER_OPTION_PIE COVER_SIZE COVER_ANCHOR COVER_PARTS COVER_OPTION_DOUGHNUT COVER_OPTION_STOCK COVER_SIZES $P2_OPTION; do
      echo "  chart_write::${!name} $(count_matches -F "fn ${!name}()" "$B/write-tests.rs")"
    done
    for name in COVER_TOOL COVER_LINE COVER_ADD_TOOL COVER_ADD_LINE COVER_TWO_TOOL COVER_3D_TOOL COVER_3D_LINE; do
      echo "  ${!name} $(count_matches -F "fn ${!name}()" "$B/null_rewrite.rs")"
    done
    # covered_once <name> <file>: the file holds the test's fn line once.
    covered_once() { [ "$(count_matches -F "fn $1()" "$2")" = 1 ]; }
    check "N1's and N2's covering crate test (the drawing refusals through add_chart, a userShapes root and a relationship whose part is missing among them) is at the phase commit, once (change ND36)" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_DRAWING" "$B/write-tests.rs")"
    # user_shapes_root: the crate test file builds a drawing whose root is
    # userShapes, the case N1 shows through the binary (change ND35).
    user_shapes_root() { [ "$(count_matches -F '<c:userShapes xmlns:c=' "$B/write-tests.rs")" -ge 1 ]; }
    check "package/tests/chart_write.rs at the phase commit builds a drawing whose root is userShapes (change ND35)" "$(yn user_shapes_root)"
    check "the tool test covering N1 is at the phase commit, once" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_TOOL" "$B/null_rewrite.rs")"
    check "the kinds tool test whose appended case is B0 is at the phase commit, once" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_LINE" "$B/null_rewrite.rs")"
    check "the tool test covering N2 is at the phase commit, once (change ND36)" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_ADD_TOOL" "$B/null_rewrite.rs")"
    check "the add-chart tool test whose appended case is B1 is at the phase commit, once (change ND36)" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_ADD_LINE" "$B/null_rewrite.rs")"
    check "CHART_TEXT_INVALID's covering crate test is at the phase commit, once" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_TEXT" "$B/write-tests.rs")"
    check "CHART_OPTION_KIND's part 4 covering crate tests (no series; a bar's Standard; a line's Clustered; an area's Clustered; a pie's second series or axis title) are at the phase commit, once each (change ND35)" "$(yn [ "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_OPTION" "$B/write-tests.rs")$(yn covered_once "$COVER_OPTION_BAR" "$B/write-tests.rs")$(yn covered_once "$COVER_OPTION_LINE" "$B/write-tests.rs")$(yn covered_once "$COVER_OPTION_AREA" "$B/write-tests.rs")$(yn covered_once "$COVER_OPTION_PIE" "$B/write-tests.rs")" = yesyesyesyesyes ])"
    check "CHART_SIZE_ANCHOR's covering crate test is at the phase commit, once" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_SIZE" "$B/write-tests.rs")"
    check "CHART_ANCHOR_OUT_OF_RANGE's covering crate test is at the phase commit, once" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_ANCHOR" "$B/write-tests.rs")"
    check "control: the same count finds no test of a planted name" "$(ynnot covered_once a_planted_test_name "$B/write-tests.rs")"
    check "the tool test covering N3 is at the phase commit, once (change ND37)" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_TWO_TOOL" "$B/null_rewrite.rs")"
    check "part 1's messages' covering crate test is at the phase commit, once (change ND37)" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_PARTS" "$B/write-tests.rs")"
    check "this phase's CHART_OPTION_KIND tests (a doughnut's hole or axis title; a stock's series count; sizes missing or misplaced) are at the phase commit, once each (change ND37)" "$(yn [ "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_OPTION_DOUGHNUT" "$B/write-tests.rs")$(yn covered_once "$COVER_OPTION_STOCK" "$B/write-tests.rs")$(yn covered_once "$COVER_SIZES" "$B/write-tests.rs")" = yesyesyes ])"
    # body_of <name> <file>: the test fn's lines, from its fn line to the
    # first line that is a lone closing brace (change ND37).
    body_of() { awk -v f="fn $1()" 'index($0, f) { on = 1 } on { print } on && $0 == "}" { exit }' "$2"; }
    # body_holds <name> <file> <text>: the test's body holds the text.
    body_holds() { [ "$(body_of "$1" "$2" | count_matches -F "$3" /dev/stdin)" -ge 1 ]; }
    # known_msg <NAME>: the message read apart for the constant.
    known_msg() { awk -F"$TAB" -v n="$1" '$1 == n { print $2 }' "$B/known.tsv"; }
    for name in NO_SUCH_PART CELL_EDIT_REPLACED REMOVED_PART_EDITED; do
      check "$name's message is a string literal of $COVER_PARTS's body (change ND37)" "$(yn body_holds "$COVER_PARTS" "$B/write-tests.rs" "\"$(known_msg "$name")\"")"
    done
    check "TWO_DRAWINGS's message is a string literal of $COVER_DRAWING's body, N3's covering crate test (change ND37)" "$(yn body_holds "$COVER_DRAWING" "$B/write-tests.rs" "\"$(known_msg TWO_DRAWINGS)\"")"
    check "TWO_DRAWINGS's message is in $COVER_TWO_TOOL's body, as the tool prints it (change ND37)" "$(yn body_holds "$COVER_TWO_TOOL" "$B/null_rewrite.rs" "\"error: $(known_msg TWO_DRAWINGS)\\n\"")"
    for name in COVER_OPTION_DOUGHNUT COVER_OPTION_STOCK COVER_SIZES; do
      check "${!name} asserts the option message, OPTION (change ND37)" "$(yn body_holds "${!name}" "$B/write-tests.rs" ", OPTION);")"
    done
    check "$COVER_SIZES asserts the text message, TEXT, for its empty sizes reference (change ND37)" "$(yn body_holds "$COVER_SIZES" "$B/write-tests.rs" ", TEXT);")"
    check "control: body_holds says no for a text the body lacks" "$(ynnot body_holds "$COVER_SIZES" "$B/write-tests.rs" "a planted text")"
    check "control: body_holds says no for a planted test name" "$(ynnot body_holds a_planted_test_name "$B/write-tests.rs" "fn")"
    body_end_ctl() { [ "$(body_of "$COVER_OPTION_STOCK" "$B/write-tests.rs" | count_matches -F "fn " /dev/stdin)" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: body_of stops at the test's closing brace, holding one fn line" "$(yn body_end_ctl)"
    check "the tool test covering N4 is at the phase commit, once (change ND38)" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_3D_TOOL" "$B/null_rewrite.rs")"
    check "the 3D tool test whose appended case is B2 is at the phase commit, once (change ND38)" "$(yn covered_once "$COVER_3D_LINE" "$B/null_rewrite.rs")"
    check "DRAWING_UNREADABLE's message is in $COVER_3D_TOOL's body, as the tool prints it (change ND38)" "$(yn body_holds "$COVER_3D_TOOL" "$B/null_rewrite.rs" "\"error: $(known_msg DRAWING_UNREADABLE)\\n\"")"
    check "$COVER_3D_TOOL's body runs the 3D sample (change ND38)" "$(yn body_holds "$COVER_3D_TOOL" "$B/null_rewrite.rs" "\"--chart-3d-sample\"")"
    # body_asserts <name> <MESSAGE>: the test's body passes the message's
    # constant to its assertion, on the call's line (", NAME);") or on a line
    # of its own ("NAME,"), as rustfmt lays it out (change ND38).
    body_asserts() { [ "$(body_of "$1" "$B/write-tests.rs" | count_matches -E "(, $2[)];\$|^[[:space:]]+$2,\$)" /dev/stdin)" -ge 1 ]; }
    for name in $P2_OPTION; do
      check "${!name} is at the phase commit, once, and asserts the option message, OPTION (change ND38)" "$(yn [ "$(yn covered_once "${!name}" "$B/write-tests.rs")$(yn body_asserts "${!name}" OPTION)" = yesyes ])"
    done
    check "$COVER_COMBINED_ORDER asserts the text message, TEXT, for the combined texts (change ND38)" "$(yn body_asserts "$COVER_COMBINED_ORDER" TEXT)"
    check "control: body_asserts says no for a constant the body does not pass" "$(ynnot body_asserts "$COVER_OPTION_LINE3D" TEXT)"
    check "control: body_asserts says no for a planted test name" "$(ynnot body_asserts a_planted_test_name OPTION)"
    printf 'fn a_planted() {\n    assert_package(\n        call(x).expect_err("refused"),\n        OPTION,\n    );\n    let OPTIONS = 1;\n}\n' >"$B/c-assert.rs"
    c_assert_ctl() { [ "$(count_matches -E "(, OPTION[)];\$|^[[:space:]]+OPTION,\$)" "$B/c-assert.rs")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same form finds a planted test's one assertion laid out on its own line, and not a name that starts with the constant's" "$(yn c_assert_ctl)"
    # held_by_tests <NAME>: the test file holds the constant's message as a
    # string literal, so its tests assert that message.
    held_by_tests() { local m; m=$(awk -F"$TAB" -v n="$1" '$1 == n { print $2 }' "$B/part.tsv"); [ -n "$m" ] && [ "$(count_matches -F "\"$m\"" "$B/write-tests.rs")" -ge 1 ]; }
    for name in $PART_NAMES; do
      check "$name's message is a string literal of package/tests/chart_write.rs" "$(yn held_by_tests "$name")"
    done
    check "control: held_by_tests says no for a constant the module does not hold" "$(ynnot held_by_tests PLANTED_NAME)"
    echo "  shown through the binary below: DRAWING_UNREADABLE by both part 4 samples, N1 (the kinds sample, a drawing whose root is not wsDr; part 4 ruling K) and N2 (the add-chart sample, a drawing relationship with no part), carried; TWO_DRAWINGS, N3 (the add-chart sample on a worksheet holding two drawing elements; part 4 ruling Q), P1's case, carried, its control B1; and DRAWING_UNREADABLE by this phase's 3D sample, N4 (N1's fixture, a drawing whose root is not wsDr; part 4 ruling K's case), its control B2; each beside its covering tests above (changes ND36 to ND38)"
    echo "  unreachable through the binary: part 1's messages for a sheet added in the same write (NO_SUCH_PART), a part this write replaces (CELL_EDIT_REPLACED) and a removed part (REMOVED_PART_EDITED): no sample adds, replaces or removes a sheet in the write that adds its chart; covered by package/tests/chart_write.rs $COVER_PARTS, whose body asserts each (change ND37)"
    echo "  unreachable through the binary: the part's four messages, each raised at the call; every sample's calls are built from the tool's own constants and are always valid, and a row past the grid meets the grid message, not one of the four:"
    echo "    CHART_TEXT_INVALID: covered by package/tests/chart_write.rs $COVER_TEXT, for the sizes reference $COVER_SIZES (change ND37), and for the secondary axis's title and format and the combined plot's series $COVER_COMBINED_ORDER (change ND38)"
    echo "    CHART_OPTION_KIND: covered by $COVER_OPTION, $COVER_OPTION_BAR, $COVER_OPTION_LINE, $COVER_OPTION_AREA and $COVER_OPTION_PIE, for P1's rules $COVER_OPTION_DOUGHNUT, $COVER_OPTION_STOCK and $COVER_SIZES (change ND37), and for this phase's rules $COVER_OPTION_LINE3D, $COVER_OPTION_AREA3D, $COVER_OPTION_PIE3D, $COVER_COMBINED_FIRST, $COVER_COMBINED_NO_AXES, $COVER_COMBINED_3D_SECOND, $COVER_COMBINED_3D_FIRST, $COVER_COMBINED_SECONDARY and $COVER_COMBINED_ORDER (change ND38)"
    echo "    CHART_SIZE_ANCHOR: covered by $COVER_SIZE"
    echo "    CHART_ANCHOR_OUT_OF_RANGE: covered by $COVER_ANCHOR"
    
    echo
    echo "## the fixtures: B0, the tool tests' appended fixture, N1 (part 4 P2's case; ruling K), N2 (part 4 P1's case) and N3 (P1's case; part 4 ruling Q); N4 is N1's through the 3D sample (this phase's case; part 4 ruling K's), B2 B0's (changes NE31 to NE38)"
    mkdir "$B/fx" || exit 2
    cat >"$B/gen-fx.py" <<'PY'
    """Fictional packages for M5 part 5 P2's negative log (change NE38): B0 is
    the tool tests' appended fixture, image_specs(A_CELL,
    "<drawing r:id=\"rId1\"/>", true) in tools/emend-copy/tests/null_rewrite.rs
    at the phase commit, rebuilt here entry by entry in its order, each entry
    stored or deflated as the test's Spec makes it (every piece of the helpers'
    source this rebuild copies is asserted present in that source); N1 is B0
    with the drawing part's root renamed from xdr:wsDr to xdr:userShapes in
    its start and end tags, stored, as the kinds tool test's refusal does
    (ruling K); N2 is B0 without the drawing part's entry, as the add-chart
    tool test's refusal removes it; N3 is B0 with the worksheet's drawing
    element written twice, as the two-drawing tool test builds it. The kinds
    tool test's expected line, one
    for both its cases, is read from the test's source (its string's
    continuations joined, its escapes read) into b0.line; the add-chart tool
    test's line for its appended case, read the same way, into b1.line;
    and the 3D tool test's line, one for both its cases, into b2.line (change
    NE38).
    Usage: gen-fx.py <null_rewrite.rs> <out dir>."""
    import os
    import re
    import sys
    import zipfile
    
    TYPES_NS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/content-types"
    RELS_NS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/package/2006/relationships"
    MAIN_NS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main"
    ATTR_NS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships"
    RELS_TYPE = "application/vnd.openxmlformats-package.relationships+xml"
    WORKBOOK_TYPE = "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet.main+xml"
    SHEET_TYPE = "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.worksheet+xml"
    STRINGS_TYPE = "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sharedStrings+xml"
    DRAWING_TYPE = "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.drawing+xml"
    XDR_NS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/spreadsheetDrawing"
    A_NS = "http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main"
    DECL = '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>'
    
    src, out = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2]
    test = open(src).read()
    
    # The expected line: the kinds test fn's one `line`, asserted for both its
    # cases, the appended one (its label, its flag and its `after`) among them.
    fn = test.index("fn the_chart_kinds_sample_adds_one_chart_of_each_kind_and_reads_them_back()")
    body = test[fn:test.index("\n}\n", fn)]
    assert re.search(r'"chart-kinds-sample-appended",\n\s*true,\n\s*"<drawing r:id=\\"rId1\\"/>",\n'
                     r'\s*\),', body), "the appended case"
    m = re.search(r'let line = "((?:[^"\\]|\\.)*)";', body, re.S)
    assert m, "the kinds test's line"
    lit = re.sub(r"\\\n\s*", "", m.group(1))
    line = lit.replace("\\t", "\t").replace("\\n", "\n")
    assert "\\" not in line and line.endswith("\n") and line.count("\n") == 1
    assert "let specs = image_specs(A_CELL, after, drawing);" in body
    assert 'assert_eq!(ran.stdout, line, "the line");' in body
    open(os.path.join(out, "b0.line"), "w").write(line.rstrip("\n"))
    print("read from null_rewrite.rs: chartkinds line fields:%d" % len(line.rstrip("\n").split("\t")))
    
    # The add-chart test's line: the string after the appended case's label, its
    # flag and its `after`, in the add-chart test fn (change NE36).
    fn = test.index("fn the_add_chart_sample_adds_a_column_chart_and_reads_it_back()")
    body = test[fn:test.index("\n}\n", fn)]
    m = re.search(r'"add-chart-sample-appended",\n\s*true,\n\s*"<drawing r:id=\\"rId1\\"/>",\n'
                  r'\s*"((?:[^"\\]|\\.)*)",\n\s*\),', body, re.S)
    assert m, "the add-chart appended case's line"
    lit = re.sub(r"\\\n\s*", "", m.group(1))
    line = lit.replace("\\t", "\t").replace("\\n", "\n")
    assert "\\" not in line and line.endswith("\n") and line.count("\n") == 1
    assert "let specs = image_specs(A_CELL, after, drawing);" in body
    open(os.path.join(out, "b1.line"), "w").write(line.rstrip("\n"))
    print("read from null_rewrite.rs: addchart line fields:%d" % len(line.rstrip("\n").split("\t")))
    
    # The 3D test's line (change NE38): the fn's one `line`, asserted for both
    # its cases, the appended one (its label, its flag and its `after`) among
    # them.
    fn = test.index("fn the_chart_3d_sample_adds_the_3d_kinds_and_a_combined_chart_and_reads_them_back()")
    body = test[fn:test.index("\n}\n", fn)]
    assert re.search(r'\("chart-3d-sample-appended", true, "<drawing r:id=\\"rId1\\"/>"\),', body), \
        "the 3D appended case"
    m = re.search(r'let line = "((?:[^"\\]|\\.)*)";', body, re.S)
    assert m, "the 3D test's line"
    lit = re.sub(r"\\\n\s*", "", m.group(1))
    line = lit.replace("\\t", "\t").replace("\\n", "\n")
    assert "\\" not in line and line.endswith("\n") and line.count("\n") == 1
    assert "let specs = image_specs(A_CELL, after, drawing);" in body
    assert 'emend_copy_with(&input, &output, &["--chart-3d-sample"]);' in body
    assert 'assert_eq!(ran.stdout, line, "the line");' in body
    open(os.path.join(out, "b2.line"), "w").write(line.rstrip("\n"))
    print("read from null_rewrite.rs: chart3d line fields:%d" % len(line.rstrip("\n").split("\t")))
    
    # The helpers' source, each piece the rebuild copies.
    for needle in [
            "fn image_specs(sheet_data: &str, after: &str, drawing: bool) -> Vec<Spec> {",
            "let mut specs = edit_specs(sheet_data);",
            "fn edit_specs(sheet_data: &str) -> Vec<Spec> {",
            "let mut specs = cells_specs();",
            "fn cells_specs() -> Vec<Spec> {",
            "let mut specs = shared_strings_specs();",
            "fn shared_strings_specs() -> Vec<Spec> {",
            'const A_CELL: &str = "<sheetData><row r=\\"1\\"><c r=\\"A1\\"><v>1</v></c></row></sheetData>";',
            '<worksheet xmlns=\\"{MAIN_NS}\\" xmlns:r=\\"{ATTR_NS}\\"><dimension ref=\\"A1\\"/>\\\n         {sheet_data}<pageMargins left=\\"0.7\\"/>{after}</worksheet>',
            '*spec = Spec::stored(b"xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml", sheet.as_bytes());',
            '<Override PartName=\\"/xl/drawings/drawing1.xml\\" \\\n                             ContentType=\\"{DRAWING_TYPE}\\"/><Override \\\n                             PartName=\\"/xl/media/image1.png\\" ContentType=\\"image/png\\"/></Types>',
            '*spec = Spec::deflated(b"[Content_Types].xml", types.as_bytes());',
            'Type=\\"{ATTR_NS}/drawing\\" Target=\\"../drawings/drawing1.xml\\"/></Relationships>',
            'b"xl/worksheets/_rels/sheet1.xml.rels",',
            'b"xl/drawings/drawing1.xml",',
            'Type=\\"{ATTR_NS}/image\\" Target=\\"../media/image1.png\\"/></Relationships>',
            'b"xl/drawings/_rels/drawing1.xml.rels",',
            'specs.push(Spec::stored(b"xl/media/image1.png", b"kept image bytes"));',
            '<si><t>alpha</t></si><si><t>a\\r\\nb</t></si></sst>',
            'Spec::deflated(b"[Content_Types].xml", content_types.as_bytes()),',
            'Spec::stored(b"_rels/.rels", package_rels.as_bytes()),',
            'Spec::deflated(b"xl/workbook.xml", workbook.as_bytes()),',
            'Spec::stored(b"xl/_rels/workbook.xml.rels", workbook_rels.as_bytes()),',
            'Spec::deflated(b"xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml", b"<sheetData/>"),',
            'Spec::deflated(b"xl/sharedStrings.xml", strings.as_bytes()),',
            '<Relationship Id=\\"rId2\\" Type=\\"{ATTR_NS}/sharedStrings\\" Target=\\"sharedStrings.xml\\"/>',
            'r:embed=\\"rId1\\"/></xdr:blipFill><xdr:spPr/></xdr:pic><xdr:clientData/>',
            '.replace("xdr:wsDr", "xdr:userShapes");',
            '*spec = Spec::stored(b"xl/drawings/drawing1.xml", text.as_bytes());',
            'specs.retain(|spec| spec.name != b"xl/drawings/drawing1.xml");',
            'fn the_add_chart_sample_refuses_a_worksheet_with_two_drawing_elements_and_leaves_nothing() {',
            '"<drawing r:id=\\"rId1\\"/><drawing r:id=\\"rId1\\"/>",',
            'fn the_chart_3d_sample_refuses_a_drawing_whose_root_is_not_ws_dr_and_leaves_nothing() {',
            'let ran = emend_copy_with(&input, &output, &["--chart-3d-sample"]);']:
        assert needle in test, needle
    print("the helpers' source pieces found: yes")
    
    STORED, DEFLATED = zipfile.ZIP_STORED, zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED
    content_types = (DECL + '<Types xmlns="' + TYPES_NS + '">'
                     '<Default Extension="rels" ContentType="' + RELS_TYPE + '"/>'
                     '<Default Extension="xml" ContentType="application/xml"/>'
                     '<Override PartName="/xl/workbook.xml" ContentType="' + WORKBOOK_TYPE + '"/>'
                     '<Override PartName="/xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml" ContentType="' + SHEET_TYPE + '"/>'
                     '<Override PartName="/xl/sharedStrings.xml" ContentType="' + STRINGS_TYPE + '"/>'
                     '<Override PartName="/xl/drawings/drawing1.xml" ContentType="' + DRAWING_TYPE + '"/>'
                     '<Override PartName="/xl/media/image1.png" ContentType="image/png"/></Types>')
    package_rels = ('<Relationships xmlns="' + RELS_NS + '"><Relationship Id="rId1" Type="' + ATTR_NS
                    + '/officeDocument" Target="xl/workbook.xml"/></Relationships>')
    workbook = ('<workbook xmlns="' + MAIN_NS + '" xmlns:r="' + ATTR_NS + '"><sheets>'
                '<sheet name="Sheet1" sheetId="1" r:id="rId1"/></sheets></workbook>')
    workbook_rels = ('<Relationships xmlns="' + RELS_NS + '">'
                     '<Relationship Id="rId1" Type="' + ATTR_NS + '/worksheet" Target="worksheets/sheet1.xml"/>'
                     '<Relationship Id="rId2" Type="' + ATTR_NS + '/sharedStrings" Target="sharedStrings.xml"/>'
                     '</Relationships>')
    strings = (DECL + '<sst xmlns="' + MAIN_NS + '" count="2" uniqueCount="2">'
               '<si><t>alpha</t></si><si><t>a\r\nb</t></si></sst>')
    sheet = (DECL + '<worksheet xmlns="' + MAIN_NS + '" xmlns:r="' + ATTR_NS + '"><dimension ref="A1"/>'
             '<sheetData><row r="1"><c r="A1"><v>1</v></c></row></sheetData><pageMargins left="0.7"/>'
             '<drawing r:id="rId1"/></worksheet>')
    sheet_rels = ('<Relationships xmlns="' + RELS_NS + '"><Relationship Id="rId1" Type="' + ATTR_NS
                  + '/drawing" Target="../drawings/drawing1.xml"/></Relationships>')
    drawing = (DECL + '<xdr:wsDr xmlns:xdr="' + XDR_NS + '" xmlns:a="' + A_NS + '"><xdr:twoCellAnchor>'
               '<xdr:from><xdr:col>3</xdr:col><xdr:colOff>0</xdr:colOff><xdr:row>3</xdr:row>'
               '<xdr:rowOff>0</xdr:rowOff></xdr:from><xdr:to><xdr:col>5</xdr:col><xdr:colOff>0'
               '</xdr:colOff><xdr:row>5</xdr:row><xdr:rowOff>0</xdr:rowOff></xdr:to><xdr:pic>'
               '<xdr:nvPicPr><xdr:cNvPr id="2" name="Picture 2"/><xdr:cNvPicPr/></xdr:nvPicPr>'
               '<xdr:blipFill><a:blip xmlns:r="' + ATTR_NS + '" '
               'r:embed="rId1"/></xdr:blipFill><xdr:spPr/></xdr:pic><xdr:clientData/>'
               '</xdr:twoCellAnchor></xdr:wsDr>')
    drawing_rels = ('<Relationships xmlns="' + RELS_NS + '"><Relationship Id="rId1" Type="' + ATTR_NS
                    + '/image" Target="../media/image1.png"/></Relationships>')
    DRAWING = "xl/drawings/drawing1.xml"
    B0 = [
        ("[Content_Types].xml", content_types.encode(), DEFLATED),
        ("_rels/.rels", package_rels.encode(), STORED),
        ("xl/workbook.xml", workbook.encode(), DEFLATED),
        ("xl/_rels/workbook.xml.rels", workbook_rels.encode(), STORED),
        ("xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml", sheet.encode(), STORED),
        ("xl/sharedStrings.xml", strings.encode(), DEFLATED),
        ("xl/worksheets/_rels/sheet1.xml.rels", sheet_rels.encode(), STORED),
        (DRAWING, drawing.encode(), STORED),
        ("xl/drawings/_rels/drawing1.xml.rels", drawing_rels.encode(), STORED),
        ("xl/media/image1.png", b"kept image bytes", STORED),
    ]
    
    
    def write(name, items):
        path = os.path.join(out, name + ".xlsx")
        with zipfile.ZipFile(path, "w") as z:
            for part, data, method in items:
                z.writestr(zipfile.ZipInfo(part, date_time=(1980, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0)), data, compress_type=method)
        with zipfile.ZipFile(path) as z:
            listed = z.namelist()
            back = all(z.read(p) == d for p, d, _ in items)
            methods = all(z.getinfo(p).compress_type == m for p, _, m in items)
        ct_index = listed.index("[Content_Types].xml") if "[Content_Types].xml" in listed else -1
        print("%s.xlsx entries:%d ct_index:%d read_back:%s methods:%s"
              % (name, len(listed), ct_index, "yes" if back else "no", "yes" if methods else "no"))
    
    
    write("b0", B0)
    renamed = []
    for part, data, method in B0:
        if part == DRAWING:
            assert data.count(b"xdr:wsDr") == 2 and b"xdr:userShapes" not in data
            data = data.replace(b"xdr:wsDr", b"xdr:userShapes")
            assert method == STORED
        renamed.append((part, data, method))
    print("n1 entries renamed:%d (the drawing part's root, xdr:wsDr to xdr:userShapes in its start and end tags, stored; every other entry as B0's)"
          % sum(1 for a, b in zip(B0, renamed) if a != b))
    write("n1", renamed)
    kept = [item for item in B0 if item[0] != DRAWING]
    print("n2 entries dropped:%d (the drawing part; the sheet's drawing element and relationship kept)"
          % (len(B0) - len(kept)))
    write("n2", kept)
    # N3 (change NE37): the worksheet's drawing element twice, the same
    # relationship named, every other entry as B0's.
    SHEET = "xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml"
    ONE = b'<drawing r:id="rId1"/>'
    doubled = []
    for part, data, method in B0:
        if part == SHEET:
            assert data.count(ONE) == 1 and method == STORED
            data = data.replace(ONE, ONE + ONE)
        doubled.append((part, data, method))
    print("n3 entries changed:%d (the worksheet, its drawing element twice; stored; every other entry as B0's)"
          % sum(1 for a, b in zip(B0, doubled) if a != b))
    write("n3", doubled)
    PY
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/gen-fx.py"
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <scratch>/w/gen-fx.py <scratch>/w/null_rewrite.rs <scratch>/w/fx"
    python3 -I -B "$B/gen-fx.py" "$B/null_rewrite.rs" "$B/fx" >"$B/gen-fx.out" 2>&1
    echo "  exit: $?"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/gen-fx.out"
    nfx=$(find "$B/fx" -type f -name '*.xlsx' | wc -l)
    echo "  fixtures written: $nfx"
    check "the four fixtures were written (B0, N1, N2 and N3; change NE37)" "$(yn [ "$nfx" = 4 ])"
    read_from_test() { [ "$(count_matches -xF "read from null_rewrite.rs: chartkinds line fields:6" "$B/gen-fx.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "the kinds tool test's line (the word and five fields), asserted for its appended case, was read from null_rewrite.rs at the phase commit" "$(yn read_from_test)"
    read_add_from_test() { [ "$(count_matches -xF "read from null_rewrite.rs: addchart line fields:10" "$B/gen-fx.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "the add-chart tool test's line for its appended case (the word and nine fields) was read from null_rewrite.rs at the phase commit (change NE36)" "$(yn read_add_from_test)"
    read_3d_from_test() { [ "$(count_matches -xF "read from null_rewrite.rs: chart3d line fields:5" "$B/gen-fx.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "the 3D tool test's line (the word and four fields), asserted for its appended case, was read from null_rewrite.rs at the phase commit (change NE38)" "$(yn read_3d_from_test)"
    check "every piece of the tool test helpers' source the rebuild copies is at the phase commit" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -xF "the helpers' source pieces found: yes" "$B/gen-fx.out")" = 1 ])"
    # differs <a> <b>: both files are there and differ by cmp.
    differs() {
      [ -s "$1" ] && [ -s "$2" ] || return 1
      if cmp -s "$1" "$2"; then return 1; fi
    }
    # fixture_ok <out> <case> <entries>: the generator's line for the case.
    fixture_ok() { [ "$(count_matches -E "^$2[.]xlsx entries:$3 ct_index:0 read_back:yes methods:yes\$" "$1")" = 1 ]; }
    check "B0 holds the tool test's ten entries, the content types part first, read back as written, each stored or deflated as the test's Spec" "$(yn fixture_ok "$B/gen-fx.out" b0 10)"
    check "N1: one entry changed, the drawing part, its root renamed to userShapes (ruling K)" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -xF "n1 entries renamed:1 (the drawing part's root, xdr:wsDr to xdr:userShapes in its start and end tags, stored; every other entry as B0's)" "$B/gen-fx.out")" = 1 ])"
    check "N1: the ten entries, read back as written" "$(yn fixture_ok "$B/gen-fx.out" n1 10)"
    check "N2: one entry dropped, the drawing part (change NE36)" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -xF "n2 entries dropped:1 (the drawing part; the sheet's drawing element and relationship kept)" "$B/gen-fx.out")" = 1 ])"
    check "N2: the nine entries, read back as written" "$(yn fixture_ok "$B/gen-fx.out" n2 9)"
    check "N3: one entry changed, the worksheet, its drawing element twice (change NE37)" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -xF "n3 entries changed:1 (the worksheet, its drawing element twice; stored; every other entry as B0's)" "$B/gen-fx.out")" = 1 ])"
    check "N3: the ten entries, read back as written" "$(yn fixture_ok "$B/gen-fx.out" n3 10)"
    check "control: fixture_ok refuses a case name no fixture line has" "$(ynnot fixture_ok "$B/gen-fx.out" n99 10)"
    check "control: fixture_ok refuses B0 with another entry count" "$(ynnot fixture_ok "$B/gen-fx.out" b0 9)"
    check "N1 differs from B0 (cmp)" "$(yn differs "$B/fx/b0.xlsx" "$B/fx/n1.xlsx")"
    check "N2 differs from B0 (cmp)" "$(yn differs "$B/fx/b0.xlsx" "$B/fx/n2.xlsx")"
    check "N2 differs from N1 (cmp)" "$(yn differs "$B/fx/n1.xlsx" "$B/fx/n2.xlsx")"
    check "N3 differs from B0, B1's fixture (cmp; change NE37)" "$(yn differs "$B/fx/b0.xlsx" "$B/fx/n3.xlsx")"
    check "control: differs says no for B0 against itself" "$(ynnot differs "$B/fx/b0.xlsx" "$B/fx/b0.xlsx")"
    check "control: differs says no for a file that is not there" "$(ynnot differs "$B/fx/b0.xlsx" "$B/fx/n99.xlsx")"
    
    # run_bin <label> <args...>: the copied binary, the command printed with the
    # paths it names, stdout, stderr and exit kept under the label.
    run_bin() {
      local label=$1
      shift
      "$BIN" "$@" >"$B/$label.stdout" 2>"$B/$label.stderr" </dev/null
      echo $? >"$B/$label.status"
      echo "command: <scratch>/w/bin/emend-copy $*"
      echo "  exit: $(cat "$B/$label.status")"
      echo "  stdout:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$B/$label.stdout"
      echo "  stderr:"; sed 's/^/    /' "$B/$label.stderr"
    }
    status_is() { [ "$(cat "$B/$1.status")" = "$2" ]; }
    refused_with() { status_is "$1" 2 && [ ! -s "$B/$1.stdout" ] && [ -n "$2" ] && [ "$(cat "$B/$1.stderr")" = "$2" ]; }
    no_output() { [ ! -e "$B/out/$1.xlsx" ]; }
    has_output() { [ -s "$B/out/$1.xlsx" ]; }
    # line_is <label> <line>: exit 0, no stderr, the line, and an output.
    line_is() { status_is "$1" 0 && [ ! -s "$B/$1.stderr" ] && [ "$(cat "$B/$1.stdout")" = "$2" ] && has_output "$1"; }
    mkdir "$B/out" || exit 2
    for case in b0 n1; do
      echo
      echo "### ${case^^} (--chart-kinds-sample)"
      run_bin "$case" "$B/fx/$case.xlsx" "$B/out/$case.xlsx" --chart-kinds-sample
    done
    # Change NE36: B1 is B0's fixture through the add-chart sample, under its own
    # label and output; N2 its refused case.
    echo
    echo "### B1 (--add-chart-sample, B0's fixture)"
    run_bin b1 "$B/fx/b0.xlsx" "$B/out/b1.xlsx" --add-chart-sample
    echo
    echo "### N2 (--add-chart-sample)"
    run_bin n2 "$B/fx/n2.xlsx" "$B/out/n2.xlsx" --add-chart-sample
    # Change NE37: N3, P1's case, its control B1 above.
    echo
    echo "### N3 (--add-chart-sample)"
    run_bin n3 "$B/fx/n3.xlsx" "$B/out/n3.xlsx" --add-chart-sample
    # Change NE38: B2 is B0's fixture through the 3D sample, under its own label
    # and output; N4, this phase's case, N1's fixture through it.
    echo
    echo "### B2 (--chart-3d-sample, B0's fixture)"
    run_bin b2 "$B/fx/b0.xlsx" "$B/out/b2.xlsx" --chart-3d-sample
    echo
    echo "### N4 (--chart-3d-sample, N1's fixture)"
    run_bin n4 "$B/fx/n1.xlsx" "$B/out/n4.xlsx" --chart-3d-sample
    echo
    echo "### the checks"
    # B0's line is the one the kinds tool test asserts for the same fixture, read
    # from null_rewrite.rs above: counts and flags only.
    L_B0=$(cat "$B/fx/b0.line")
    echo "  B0's expected line, from the kinds tool test, asserted for its appended case:"
    printf '%s\n' "$L_B0" | sed 's/^/    /'
    check "B0: exit 0, the kinds tool test's line, an output (the control for N1; ruling K)" "$(yn line_is b0 "$L_B0")"
    L_B1=$(cat "$B/fx/b1.line")
    echo "  B1's expected line, from the add-chart tool test's appended case (change NE36):"
    printf '%s\n' "$L_B1" | sed 's/^/    /'
    check "B1: exit 0, the add-chart tool test's line, an output (the control for N2 and N3; changes NE36 and NE37)" "$(yn line_is b1 "$L_B1")"
    L_B2=$(cat "$B/fx/b2.line")
    echo "  B2's expected line, from the 3D tool test, asserted for its appended case (change NE38):"
    printf '%s\n' "$L_B2" | sed 's/^/    /'
    check "B2: exit 0, the 3D tool test's line, an output (the control for N4; change NE38)" "$(yn line_is b2 "$L_B2")"
    : >"$B/reached"
    # refusal <case> <NAME> <what>: the case refused with the message of NAME,
    # no output.
    refusal() {
      local case=$1 name=$2 what=$3 expect
      expect=$(msg "$name")
      check "${case^^} ($what): exit 2, no stdout, the error line exactly the $name message" "$(yn refused_with "$case" "$expect")"
      check "${case^^}: no output file" "$(yn no_output "$case")"
      if refused_with "$case" "$expect"; then
        printf '%s\n' "$case" >>"$B/reached"
      fi
    }
    refusal n1 DRAWING_UNREADABLE "part 4 P2's: the kinds sample on a drawing whose root is not wsDr; ruling K"
    refusal n2 DRAWING_UNREADABLE "part 4 P1's: the add-chart sample on a drawing relationship with no part"
    refusal n3 TWO_DRAWINGS "P1's: the add-chart sample on a worksheet holding two drawing elements; part 4 ruling Q"
    refusal n4 DRAWING_UNREADABLE "this phase's: the 3D sample on a drawing whose root is not wsDr; part 4 ruling K's case"
    echo "  refused as expected, by case:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/reached"
    check "the 4 cases were refused, N1, N2, N3 and N4 (change NE38)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$B/reached")" = 4 ])"
    b0_refused() { refused_with b0 "$(msg DRAWING_UNREADABLE)"; }
    check "control: refused_with says no on B0's run" "$(ynnot b0_refused)"
    b1_refused() { refused_with b1 "$(msg DRAWING_UNREADABLE)"; }
    check "control: refused_with says no on B1's run" "$(ynnot b1_refused)"
    b1_two_refused() { refused_with b1 "$(msg TWO_DRAWINGS)"; }
    check "control: refused_with says no on B1's run against N3's message (change NE37)" "$(ynnot b1_two_refused)"
    n3_other() { refused_with n3 "$(msg DRAWING_UNREADABLE)"; }
    check "control: refused_with says no on N3's run against the drawing message (change NE37)" "$(ynnot n3_other)"
    b2_refused() { refused_with b2 "$(msg DRAWING_UNREADABLE)"; }
    check "control: refused_with says no on B2's run (change NE38)" "$(ynnot b2_refused)"
    n4_other() { refused_with n4 "$(msg TWO_DRAWINGS)"; }
    check "control: refused_with says no on N4's run against the two-drawing message (change NE38)" "$(ynnot n4_other)"
    empty_message() { refused_with n1 ""; }
    check "control: refused_with says no against an empty message" "$(ynnot empty_message)"
    other_message() { refused_with n1 "error: a worksheet has two drawing elements"; }
    check "control: refused_with says no on N1's run against another message" "$(ynnot other_message)"
    b0_line_ctl() { line_is b0 "$(printf '%s' "$L_B0" | sed "s/${TAB}charts_after=6${TAB}/${TAB}charts_after=7${TAB}/")"; }
    check "control: line_is says no on B0's run against a line with one chart more" "$(ynnot b0_line_ctl)"
    b0_line_changes() { [ "$(printf '%s' "$L_B0" | sed "s/${TAB}charts_after=6${TAB}/${TAB}charts_after=7${TAB}/")" != "$L_B0" ]; }
    check "control: the planted line differs from B0's" "$(yn b0_line_changes)"
    b1_line_ctl() { line_is b1 "$(printf '%s' "$L_B1" | sed "s/${TAB}charts_after=1${TAB}/${TAB}charts_after=2${TAB}/")"; }
    check "control: line_is says no on B1's run against a line with one chart more" "$(ynnot b1_line_ctl)"
    b1_line_changes() { [ "$(printf '%s' "$L_B1" | sed "s/${TAB}charts_after=1${TAB}/${TAB}charts_after=2${TAB}/")" != "$L_B1" ]; }
    check "control: the planted line differs from B1's" "$(yn b1_line_changes)"
    b2_line_ctl() { line_is b2 "$(printf '%s' "$L_B2" | sed "s/${TAB}charts_after=5${TAB}/${TAB}charts_after=6${TAB}/")"; }
    check "control: line_is says no on B2's run against a line with one chart more (change NE38)" "$(ynnot b2_line_ctl)"
    b2_line_changes() { [ "$(printf '%s' "$L_B2" | sed "s/${TAB}charts_after=5${TAB}/${TAB}charts_after=6${TAB}/")" != "$L_B2" ]; }
    check "control: the planted line differs from B2's" "$(yn b2_line_changes)"
    cross_3d_ctl() { line_is b2 "$L_B0"; }
    check "control: line_is says no on B2's run against the kinds line" "$(ynnot cross_3d_ctl)"
    out_3d_ctl() { line_is n4 ""; }
    check "control: line_is says no on N4's refused run, which left no output" "$(ynnot out_3d_ctl)"
    cross_ctl() { line_is b1 "$L_B0"; }
    check "control: line_is says no on B1's run against the kinds line" "$(ynnot cross_ctl)"
    out_ctl() { line_is n1 ""; }
    check "control: line_is says no on N1's refused run, which left no output" "$(ynnot out_ctl)"
    nout=$(find "$B/out" -type f | wc -l)
    echo "  output files: $nout, the accepted runs' (B0, B1 and B2)"
    check "no output but the three accepted runs', and no temporary beside them (change NE38)" "$(yn [ "$nout" = 3 ])"
    
    
    echo
    echo "## the log itself"
    ALL=()
    for f in "$B"/*.stdout "$B"/*.stderr "$B"/*.out; do ALL+=("$f"); done
    nbytes=$(cat "${ALL[@]}" | LC_ALL=C tr -cd '\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177\200-\377' | wc -c)
    printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m y caf\303\251\n' >"$B/ctl-bytes"
    nctl=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd '\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177\200-\377' <"$B/ctl-bytes" | wc -c)
    echo "  captured outputs: ${#ALL[@]}; control and non-ASCII bytes in them: $nbytes; in a control file with two ESC and one two-byte character: $nctl"
    check "no control or non-ASCII byte in any captured output" "$(yn [ "$nbytes" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same count finds four bytes in the control file" "$(yn [ "$nctl" = 4 ])"
    echo "command: git status --porcelain"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    st_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    st_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    echo "status lines: $st_all; of them admitted by the phase's pattern (this phase's logs, its records, planning's modified specs/0036): $st_ours"
    status_accounted() { [ "$st_all" != error ] && [ "$st_ours" != error ] && [ "$st_all" = "$st_ours" ]; }
    check "every change in the working tree is admitted by the phase's pattern: this phase's logs, its records or planning's modified specs/0036" "$(yn status_accounted)"
    echo
    echo "## this run's directory removed (change HC)"
    echo "command: rm -rf <scratch>/w (this run's own mktemp -d directory, written \"\${B:?}\")"
    rm -rf "${B:?}"
    b_present() { [ -e "$B" ]; }
    check "<scratch>/w is gone" "$(ynnot b_present)"
    check "control: the same test finds <build>, which stays" "$(yn test -e "$BUILD_ROOT")"
    echo
    echo "## this script's own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    nerr=$(wc -c <"$ERR")
    # Change MW (ruling 12): the copy with one byte appended is counted
    # through a pipe, so no plain file is made.
    nerr_ctl=$({ cat "$ERR"; printf 'x'; } | wc -c)
    echo "  command: wc -c <scripts>/out/negative.stderr: $nerr bytes; a copy with one byte appended: $nerr_ctl"
    check "this script wrote nothing to its standard error" "$(yn [ "$nerr" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same count reads one byte more in the copy" "$(yn [ "$nerr_ctl" = "$((nerr + 1))" ])"
    echo "run ended at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    echo "negative log checks all as expected: $([ "$fail" -eq 0 ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    exec 1>&3
    wait "$SCRUB_PID" 2>/dev/null
    exit "$fail"

## the shared counting library this log sources
    # emend shared counting forms (specs/0007-gate-self-test.md, "scripts/counting.sh").
    #
    # Sourced by scripts/gate-self-test.sh and by the log scripts of later phases,
    # which use these instead of carrying their own copy.
    #
    # WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. In T3 P4 four counting sites compared a bare `grep -c`
    # with 0 without reading the exit status, so a read error printed 0 and the
    # check passed. Two independent checks found them, and the class was declared
    # closed three further times while instances still stood: a helper whose first
    # repair read grep's status while `cat` was the failing command, and both
    # halves of one function in T2 P7. Planning's remedy is that every counting
    # form, including a throwaway one, is a named function that reads the exit
    # status and has a positive control, from the start.
    #
    # Every function prints either a number or the word "error". None of them ever
    # prints a matched line, a value, or a path. A caller that compares a result
    # with 0 therefore cannot mistake a failed read for an absence.
    #
    # counting_controls runs every form against a match, a miss and an unreadable
    # file, prints one line per control, and sets counting_controls_ok. Callers run
    # it before using any form.
    
    G=/usr/bin/grep
    
    # count_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: total matching lines across the
    # files, or "error" if any file could not be read. The files go to grep
    # directly: with `cat file | grep -c`, an unreadable file makes CAT fail while
    # grep counts 0 over the empty stream and exits 1, so the read error reads as
    # "no hits".
    count_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_from_file <-F|-E> <pattern file> <file>...: the same, with the patterns
    # read from a file (grep -f), so a pattern is never printed.
    count_from_file() {
      local mode=$1 patterns=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -f "$patterns" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_bytes <tr class> <file>...: total bytes of that class across the files,
    # or "error" if any file could not be read. Each file is read on its own rather
    # than through `cat "$@" | tr`, for the same reason as above.
    count_bytes() {
      local class=$1 total=0 f n
      shift
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd "$class" <"$f" | wc -c) || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_lines <file>...: total lines, or "error" if any file could not be read.
    count_lines() {
      local total=0 f n
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(wc -l <"$f") || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_matches_i <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: count_matches with -i, the form
    # the hygiene step uses for OFFICE_RE and ZONE_RE. It lived in a log script as a
    # hand-rolled copy with no control of its own (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap
    # 14); a counting form belongs here, with a control, even a throwaway one.
    count_matches_i() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c -i "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # run_lines <command...>: run the command, and print the number of lines it
    # wrote on stdout, or "error" if the command itself failed. The log scripts
    # asserted a clean working tree with
    #   git status --porcelain >file 2>/dev/null || : >file
    # which turns a FAILED git status into an empty file, so the check read a
    # failed command as a clean tree (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap 1; planning
    # reproduced it). Reading the command's exit status is the whole point: a
    # command that could not run is never the same as a command that found nothing.
    run_lines() {
      local out rc
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | wc -l | tr -d ' '
    }
    
    # run_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <command...>: the same, counting only the lines
    # that match, so a caller can compare "all lines" with "lines of the expected
    # shape" without either count hiding a failed command.
    run_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" || true
    }
    
    CTRL_CLASS='\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177'
    NONASCII_CLASS='\200-\377'
    
    # counting_controls <label prefix>: run every counting form above against a
    # fixture that must match and one that must not, and against an unreadable
    # file, printing one line per result. Sets counting_controls_ok to yes or no.
    # This is the positive control planning requires for every form, and it also
    # proves each form reports "error" rather than 0 when it cannot read.
    counting_controls() {
      local d ok=yes r
      d=$(mktemp -d) || { counting_controls_ok=no; return; }
      printf 'alpha\nbeta needle gamma\nneedle\n' >"$d/hit"
      printf 'nothing of interest\n' >"$d/miss"
      printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m\017 y\ncaf\303\251\n' >"$d/bytes"
      printf 'needle\n' >"$d/patterns"
      printf 'unreadable\n' >"$d/locked"
      chmod 000 "$d/locked"
    
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit");        echo "  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/miss");       echo "  control count_matches on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_matches summed over two files: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -E 'ne+dle' "$d/hit");      echo "  control count_matches with a regular expression: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/locked");     echo "  control count_matches on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_matches on readable plus unreadable: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/hit"); echo "  control count_from_file on the same file: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_from_file on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_from_file on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/bytes");    echo "  control count_bytes, control bytes in a file with ESC, ESC and SI: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$d/bytes"); echo "  control count_bytes, non-ASCII bytes in a file with one two-byte character: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/miss");     echo "  control count_bytes on a clean file: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_bytes on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/hit");                    echo "  control count_lines on a three-line file: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/locked");                 echo "  control count_lines on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      printf 'NEEDLE\nneedle\n' >"$d/mixedcase"
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/mixedcase"); echo "  control count_matches_i on mixed case: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/mixedcase");  echo "  control count_matches on the same file, case sensitive: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_matches_i on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines printf 'a\nb\nc\n');            echo "  control run_lines on a command printing three lines: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines true);                          echo "  control run_lines on a command printing nothing: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines false);                         echo "  control run_lines on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines "$d/no-such-command");          echo "  control run_lines on a command that cannot run: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle printf 'needle\nother\n'); echo "  control run_matches on a command printing one match: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle false);             echo "  control run_matches on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
    
      chmod 644 "$d/locked"
      rm -rf "${d:?}"
      counting_controls_ok=$ok
      echo "  counting controls: $([ "$ok" = yes ] && echo "all as expected" || echo FAILED)"
    }

